<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Package xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
    Disposition LOI stage narrowing (user request, 2026-08-21): "Received, under review,
    negotiations, Signed" replaces the five-stage Received -> Under Review -> Countered by
    DPEG -> Counter Received from Buyer -> Executed sequence on the Disposition_LOI record
    type. See agent-output/disposition-loi-stages.md for the full design and
    objects/LOI__c/recordTypes/Disposition_LOI.recordType-meta.xml's 2026-08-21 retraction
    block for the live change record.

    STATUS: PREPARED, NOT AUTHORISED. Do not deploy without the user's explicit go-ahead.
    This file only DESCRIBES a deletion; it performs nothing on its own.

    Retires the two-quick-action negotiation LOOP the old sequence needed (we counter, the
    buyer counters back) and is no longer needed now the loop is retired: negotiation rounds,
    in either direction, are recorded on Counter History (Counter_Offer__c / c/loiCounterOffer,
    UNCHANGED) while the record sits at a single 'Negotiation' stage.

    DELETES 2 QUICK ACTIONS AND 2 LWC BUNDLES:
      QuickAction:
        - LOI__c.Mark_Countered_By_DPEG   (LWC: loiMarkCounteredByDpeg)
        - LOI__c.Mark_Counter_Received    (LWC: loiMarkCounterReceived)
      LightningComponentBundle:
        - loiMarkCounteredByDpeg
        - loiMarkCounterReceived

    POST-destructive (not pre-): flexipages/LOI_Record_Page.flexipage-meta.xml's two
    <valueListItems> entries referencing these quick actions are already removed in the
    companion constructive payload, so by the time this file's deletions run, nothing in the
    constructive payload still references the components being deleted. Deleting a quick
    action that is still referenced by a live FlexiPage <valueListItems> block fails the
    delete - POST ordering is what avoids that, exactly as manifest/portfolio-deal-b4's
    destructiveChangesPost.xml already established for this repo's LWC-bundle-rename pattern.

    NOT deleted here, and deliberately so: 'Countered by DPEG' and 'Counter Received from
    Buyer' stay ACTIVE on the master LOI__c.Stage__c picklist (orphaned, on no record type -
    see that field's own 2026-08-21 retraction) - deactivating them is a further, separate
    decision this wave does not make. Counter_Offer__c, c/loiCounterOffer, and every other
    LOI__c quick action (Advance_Stage, Edit_LOI, Mark_Completed, Mark_Countered,
    Submit_for_Approval) are unaffected.

    THE package.xml IN THIS SAME FOLDER IS A TEST HARNESS ONLY, NOT THE REAL DEPLOY MANIFEST.
    sf's --post-destructive-changes flag requires --manifest to be passed alongside it (cannot
    be combined with a plain --source-dir deploy), so this folder's package.xml is an
    intentionally EMPTY constructive manifest (<types> omitted entirely) whose only job is to
    let this destructive file be check-only validated in isolation. Per the design doc's §5.2,
    the REAL deploy ships this as ONE atomic payload with the whole constructive change set
    (A1-A10 declarative, D1-D12 Apex/LWC) via --source-dir, paired with this same
    --post-destructive-changes file. The master manifest/package.xml is also updated in this
    same wave (four <members> lines removed: the two LWC bundle names and the two QuickAction
    fullNames this file deletes) so a future retrieve does not resurrect them.

    Deploy (only once authorised by the user; devops runs a validation-only dry-run first per
    standing project practice):
      sf project deploy start \
        --source-dir force-app \
        --post-destructive-changes manifest/loi-disposition-stage-narrow/destructiveChangesPost.xml \
        --target-org usman-dpeg \
        --test-level RunLocalTests --wait 30

    Do NOT pass --purge-on-delete - documented elsewhere in this repo as non-functional on
    production orgs and fails silently rather than erroring (see manifest/portfolio-deal-a3).

    Rollback: deleted QuickActions and LWC bundles are recoverable from git history (this same
    wave removes them from force-app/main/default), but are NOT recoverable from any org-side
    recycle bin the way custom fields are - QuickAction/LWC deletions are not soft-deleted by
    the platform. Re-deploying the old source and restoring flexipages/LOI_Record_Page's two
    <valueListItems> entries would restore function.
    -->
    <types>
        <members>LOI__c.Mark_Countered_By_DPEG</members>
        <members>LOI__c.Mark_Counter_Received</members>
        <name>QuickAction</name>
    </types>
    <types>
        <members>loiMarkCounteredByDpeg</members>
        <members>loiMarkCounterReceived</members>
        <name>LightningComponentBundle</name>
    </types>
    <version>67.0</version>
</Package>
